                   <elementSpec ident="lb" module="core" mode="change">
                       <desc versionDate="2014-06-09" xml:lang="en">marks the beginning of a line of prose, including the first line of a paragraph. Although formally defined as ‘line break’, it is more usefully thought of as ‘line beginning’. <gi>lb</gi> should be sparingly used within the Darwin Correspondence to indicate a linebreak within the original letter text that we wish to preserve within the output.</desc>
                       <classes mode="change">
                           <memberOf key="att.breaking" mode="delete"/>
                           <memberOf key="att.edition" mode="delete"/>
                           <memberOf key="att.spanning" mode="delete"/>
                       </classes>
                       <attList>
                           <attDef ident="n" mode="change">
                               <!--NEW-->
                           </attDef>
                           <attDef ident="rend" mode="change">
                               <!--NEW-->
                           </attDef>
                           <attDef ident="resp" usage="opt" mode="change"/>
                           <attDef ident="type" mode="change">
                               <!--NEW-->
                           </attDef>
                           <attDef ident="ana" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="cert" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="change" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="copyOf" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="corresp" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="exclude" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="facs" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="next" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="prev" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="rendition" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="sameAs" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="select" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="source" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="style" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="synch" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:base" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:id" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:lang" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:space" mode="delete"/>
                       </attList>
                       <exemplum xml:lang="en">
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
                               <p>With much respect, I beg to remain | Your’s faithfully | Ch. Darwin <lb type="none"/> His Excellency | Sir G.&#160;Grey | &amp;amp;c &amp;amp;c &amp;amp;c</p>
                           </egXML>
                       </exemplum>
                       <exemplum xml:lang="en">
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
                               <p rend="left">Charles Darwin Esq. M.A. | Down, Beckenham. | Kent. <lb type="full"/> **Such as the following:—</p>
                           </egXML>
                       </exemplum>
                       <remarks versionDate="2014-05-21" xml:lang="en">
                           <p>Where <gi>lb</gi> occurs between two words, one space should be left before it. Where it divides a single word or occurs at the beginning of a paragraph, there should be no space on either side of it.</p>
                           <p>If you find yourself wanting to insert forced linebreaks at the very end of a paragraph (a common usage in DarML), please consult the Guidelines on paragraph (or block) styling on how to indicate that a pargraph has extra (or no) linebreaks immediately before it. If you are trying to insert forced linebreaks in parts of the metadata, please contact Michael Hawkins as this might indicate the need to update the code that renders our materials in print and online.</p>
                       </remarks>
                   </elementSpec>
                   
                   <elementSpec module="core" ident="lg" mode="change">
                       <!--DROP?-->
                       <classes mode="change">
                           <memberOf key="att.declaring" mode="delete"/>
                           <memberOf key="att.divLike" mode="delete"/>
                           <memberOf key="att.global" mode="delete"/>
                           <memberOf key="att.typed" mode="delete"/>
                       </classes>
                       <exemplum xml:lang="en">
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
                               <lg>
                                   <l>Now that his new book has come out,</l>
                                   <l>I find that dreadful man</l>
                                   <l>Is trying to heap on us</l>
                                   <l>Every insult that he can.</l>
                               </lg>
                           </egXML>
                       </exemplum>
                       <remarks xml:lang="en" versionDate="2022-07-05">
                           <p><hi rend="bold">NB:</hi> This element is only used in three files, all made before the switch to TEI. Review usage to ensure that it conforms to actual DCP editorial practice. Are these the only examples of verse or have other occurrences been coded simply as paragraphs using <gi>p</gi>.</p>
                       </remarks>
                   </elementSpec>
                   
                   <elementSpec ident="list" module="core" mode="change">
                       <desc versionDate="2014-06-17" xml:lang="en">contains any number of items organised as a list.</desc>
                       <classes mode="change">
                           <memberOf key="att.sortable" mode="delete"/>
                       </classes>
                       <attList>
                           <attDef ident="rend" mode="change" usage="opt">
                               <desc versionDate="2014-06-09" xml:lang="en">used to indicate how the list should be rendered. Valid values include ‘<val>bulleted</val> (with bullets) ’, ‘<val>ordered</val> (numbered with Arabic or Roman numbers or letters) ’ or ‘<val>simple</val>’ (no markers for each item).</desc>
                               <valList type="closed" mode="replace">
                                   <valItem ident="bulleted"/>
                                   <valItem ident="ordered"/>
                                   <valItem ident="simple"/>
                               </valList>
                               <remarks versionDate="2014-06-11" xml:lang="en">
                                   <p>This element is used only rarely by the Darwin Project. It is typically to encode formulaic lists, clearly set out as such in the original.</p>
                                   <p>Should an atypical form of bulleting be used in the original (and desired to be reproduced in the print/online versions, please contact Michael Hawkins how it can be supported.</p>
                               </remarks>
                           </attDef>
                           <attDef ident="type" mode="change">
                               <!--NEW-->
                           </attDef>
                           <attDef ident="ana" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="cert" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="change" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="copyOf" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="corresp" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="exclude" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="facs" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="n" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="next" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="prev" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="rendition" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="resp" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="sameAs" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="select" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="source" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="style" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="subtype" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="synch" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:base" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:id" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:lang" mode="delete"/>
                           <attDef ident="xml:space" mode="delete"/>
                       </attList>
                       <exemplum xml:lang="en">
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
                               <list type="simple">
                                   <item>“intense cobalt Blue”</item>
                                   <item>“silver yellow”</item>
                                   <item>“deep copper red”</item>
                               </list>
                           </egXML>
                       </exemplum>
                       <exemplum xml:lang="en">
                           <egXML xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/Examples">
                               <list rend="block">
                                   <item><label>1.</label> Scalpellum trilineatum— Chalk. Marl</item>
                                   <item><label>2)</label> S.&#160;do <hi rend="underline">or</hi> S.&#160;fossula, upper Chalk</item>
                                   <item><label>3</label> S.——— fossula (?) Upper chalk</item>
                                   <item>Scalpellum maximum Upper Chalk</item>
                                   <item><label>4</label> S.&#160;lineatum of Lower Chalk <hi rend="underline">or</hi> var of S.&#160;arcuatum of Chalk Marl. 7&#160;to</item>
                                   <item><label>5</label> many valves of Pollicipes glaber.</item>
                               </list>
                           </egXML>
                       </exemplum>
                       <remarks versionDate="2014-06-11" xml:lang="en">
                           <p>This element is used only rarely by the Darwin Project. It istypically to encode formulaic lists, clearly set out as such in the original.</p>
                           <p>Should an atypical form of bulleting be used in the original (and desired to be reproduced in the print/online versions, please contact Michael Hawkins how it can be supported.</p>
                           <p>Some <gi>list</gi> currently have <att>type</att> with a value of "<val>ordered</val>". These should be manually fixed with the numbers (and any punctuation after them) coded using <gi>label</gi>.</p>
                       </remarks>
                   </elementSpec>
                   
                   <elementSpec module="core" ident="measure" mode="change">
